.TH LDLM.LOCKDEP 4 2026-09-23 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
ldlm.lockdep \- lock order checker for server inodebits locks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param ldlm.lockdep=" 0|1
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param ldlm.lockdep_epoch=" LABEL
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param ldlm.lockdep_pause=" 0|1
.SY
.B "lctl get_param ldlm.lockdep_cycles ldlm.lockdep_rerequests"
.SY
.B "lctl get_param ldlm.lockdep_stats ldlm.lockdep_reports"
.SY
.B "lctl get_param ldlm.lockdep_graph"
.SY
.B "lctl set_param ldlm.lockdep_selftest=1"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR ldlm.lockdep ", " ldlm.lockdep_epoch ", " ldlm.lockdep_pause :
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.br
.BR ldlm.lockdep_cycles ", " ldlm.lockdep_rerequests ", "
.BR ldlm.lockdep_stats ", " ldlm.lockdep_reports ", " ldlm.lockdep_graph :
.BR 444 " | " -r--r--r--
.br
.BR ldlm.lockdep_selftest :
.BR 200 " | " --w-------
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Global, on a server
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB ldlm.lockdep= 0
.SH DESCRIPTION
The checker records, for each request handler or server thread, the
inodebits locks it is granted on the local enqueue path and through OSP.
A request that waits for its grant while others are held adds edges to a
graph of call sites and to a graph of resources, and a new edge that
closes a cycle is reported.
A second waiting request on a resource already held is reported under
rule 1 when it conflicts with the hold, or when a request that could be
queued between them has been seen.
Only mandatory bits are wanted, and tries and requests whose completion
does not wait add no edges.
The checker never blocks, fails or panics an operation; a test decides
failure from the counters and the reports.
It is meant for test systems: every enqueue takes a stack trace and a
global lock while it is on.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep
turns the checker on or off.
Turning it off forgets every hold and report.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep_epoch
starts new, empty graphs under
.IR LABEL ,
keeping the holds.
Set the same label on every server before a test's actors run.
Reading it shows the epoch number and label.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep_pause
keeps tracking holds but adds nothing to the graphs.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep_cycles
counts the epoch's class order, resource conflict and queue-bridged cycle
reports.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep_rerequests
counts the epoch's rule 1 reports that conflict with the hold or have a
bridge.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep_stats
shows the counts of each report category, the use of each bounded table,
and every loss.
.B complete: 1
means that nothing was dropped in this epoch.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep_reports
lists every report with its witness: the call sites, modes, bits and
resources of each edge, each resource named with the target that owns its
lock namespace.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep_graph
streams both graphs, for merging the graphs of several servers.
.TP
.B ldlm.lockdep_selftest
runs the graph searches on built graphs; the write fails if any case
fails, and the console names it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Turn the checker on, start a labelled epoch, and read its cycle count:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl set_param ldlm.lockdep=1"
.RB mds# " lctl set_param ldlm.lockdep_epoch=sanityn-123a"
.RB mds# " lctl get_param -n ldlm.lockdep_cycles"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B ldlm.lockdep
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" commit v2_17_58
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lctl (8)
